-- 106: Filling the rule gaps (US plan step 4): Kansas, Nebraska, Massachusetts, Rhode Island, Maine (no rows before), and trout / salmon for
-- Michigan, Wisconsin and Indiana (setup/100 had none).
-- Checked 2026-10-22 in each state's own guide (links in source_url): Kansas Fishing Regulations Summary 2026 (ksoutdoors.gov, statewide creel and
-- length limits p. 9); Nebraska 2026 Fishing Guide (outdoornebraska.gov, regulations by species); Massachusetts freshwater regulations (mass.gov,
-- updated Sep 25, 2026) and the 2026 Massachusetts saltwater guide (DMF's official guide on eRegulations, updated Oct 5, 2026); Rhode Island 2026
-- freshwater and saltwater guides (DEM's official guides on eRegulations, updated Sep 23 and Oct 5, 2026); Maine 2026 Fishing Laws & Rules
-- (maine.gov/ifw, general law p. 2) and Maine DMR's 2026 Striped Bass (Mar 25, 2026) and Saltwater Recreational Fishing (Jul 1, 2026) sheets;
-- 2026 Michigan Fishing Regulations (Great Lakes trout & salmon p. 18-21, inland trout & salmon p. 42-43); Wisconsin Trout Fishing Regulations
-- 2026-2027 and the Guide to Wisconsin Hook and Line Fishing Regulations 2026-2027 (Lake Michigan p. 88-90, Lake Superior p. 91-93);
-- Indiana 2026 Fishing Regulation Guide (inland trout p. 20, Lake Michigan p. 22).
-- A state rule is a normal fish_rules row whose `regions` holds the 2-letter state code. Needs setup/94 first (its check already allows these codes).
-- Where a rule changes by area, zone, season or water the app can only show one number, so the STRICTER one is the size and the note has the rest
-- (an area like Lake Superior or south of Cape Cod counts; single named lakes and listed trout-water types do not, as before).
-- Closed dates are only added where the main way of fishing for that fish closes, written as the stretch that is closed in every year.
-- NOT added: lobster and crabs (shell sizes), paddlefish (special tags and snagging seasons), Kansas lake-by-lake limits, Nebraska listed lakes.
-- Insert only; no delete / drop.

insert into fish_rules (species, match, regions, min_in, max_in, measure, one_over, bag, release_only, closed, open_only, note, source_url, verified_on, active) values
